      "message": "Turns out that these two x86 files comes from objects under `tools/bpf/resolve_btfids`. After building the Pixel build, the program discovers objects under that directory using these headers. The complete list:\n\n```\n    \"common/tools/include/uapi/asm/../../../arch/x86/include/uapi/asm/bitsperlong.h\": [\n        \"tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/.ctype.o\",\n        \"tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/.main.o\",\n        \"tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/.rbtree.o\",\n        \"tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/.str_error_r.o\",\n        \"tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/.string.o\"\n    ],\n    \"common/tools/include/uapi/asm/../../../arch/x86/include/uapi/asm/errno.h\": [\n        \"tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/.main.o\",\n        \"tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/.string.o\"\n    ],\n```\n\nI can add logic in my script to drop these headers, but I just want to confirm that we definitely don\u0027t want these to sneak in.",
